   626	3. WHEN TO PROPOSE A NEW THESIS
   627	
   628	A thesis is a question a senior analyst would hold a card for: its answer could change a position because it could change the
   629	company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk, or competitive position in a way you can name; public material will settle it on a
   630	date; and no open thesis already asks it. A thesis asks one quantity for one period, or one event. It opens for one of four reasons, a closed set; a matter that fits none of them is
   631	evidence, kept and linked to the theses it informs or left unlinked, never a thesis:
   632	- product_node: when the generation of the main product that carries the company's value reaches the step that brings revenue,
   633	  usually first shipments; announcements and samples are its evidence, and only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's
   634	  trial result and its approval) are separate theses ("will the carmaker's new platform start deliveries in 2026?";
   635	  "will the drugmaker's next-generation inhaler, the product line that carries its value, reach pharmacies by mid-2027?").
   636	- binding_obligation: an obligation the company takes on in its own name, large enough to change its revenue, profit, cash or credit
   637	  risk: guaranteeing, backing or giving credit support for another party's debt, lease, revenue or capacity, lending to it,
   638	  committing to buy capacity or services, or a sized stake or acquisition not yet completed. One already undertaken is tracked by its
   639	  amount at the next annual report; one not yet signed by whether it is signed by a check date within 18 months of the item ("how much will the
   640	  utility have guaranteed for its project companies' loans at its next annual report?"; "will the retailer sign a guarantee for its
   641	  franchisees' leases, large enough to change its credit risk, by the check date?"). Its own borrowing or leases and a completed
   642	  or unsized investment are not obligations.
   643	- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:
   644	  several companies' combined output or spending, a contract price, an interest rate ("the largest container lines' combined capacity
   645	  added in 2026"; "next year's average contract price of a raw material"). Another population or wording of the same aggregate is
   646	  evidence for it.
   647	- policy_stage: the step a policy or regulatory process reaches, naming who decides ("will the regulator approve the drug for a second
   648	  indication?"; "will the government require licences for the product's exports by a date?").
   649	
   650	- Open only matters an analyst would bet on separately; small matters open no thesis and their statements are kept as evidence. A
   651	  customer's deployment plan is evidence for the company's demand and product theses, unless it changes the company's own cash or
   652	  credit risk, which is judged as an obligation.
   653	- Give the date the item supports. When it gives none, use the date the reason fixes and say how it was set: an obligation already
   654	  undertaken, its next annual report; an unsigned obligation, a check date within 18 months of the item; a pending regulatory
   655	  decision, the current fiscal year-end. A shared quantity takes its release date and a product event the date its outcome can be
   656	  checked, only when the item supports one. A question no date can settle is rewritten or not opened.
   657	- Do not open a thesis about: an executive appointment or organisational change; the company's own borrowing or leases as an
   658	  obligation; a buyback authorisation or dividend declaration; a financial measure's level, growth, margin or guidance for any period,
   659	  on its own; an undated moat or strategy; a feature, content or software update, price point, regional service or variant of a
   660	  product already on sale; another estimate, source or wording of what an open thesis tracks; an annual quantity after next year (an
   661	  obligation excepted); shareholder votes, bylaws or routine litigation procedure. Their statements are evidence for the theses they
   662	  inform, or left unlinked.
   663	- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest
   664	  open thesis with why an analyst would bet on the two separately because their answers can move apart; with no open thesis, say so.
   665	  If the two cannot move apart, link the evidence to every open thesis it informs instead.
   666	
   712	
   713	Return the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty
   714	lists when nothing passes.
   715	```
